<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Codecov: FAQ and troubleshooting" id="Codecov-FAQ">

    <primary-label ref="codecov"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <link-summary>Answers to common Codecov plugin questions: missing coverage, repository detection, connection errors, validation and bug reports.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Solutions for missing coverage, connection errors and validation problems.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Troubleshoot the Codecov plugin in JetBrains IDEs: missing coverage, undetected repositories, failed connection tests, empty dashboards and validation.</web-summary>

    <chapter title="Why can't I see coverage for my branch?" id="missing-coverage">
        <p>
            The editor gutter shows the coverage of the latest Codecov report on the repository's default branch, not of your current branch.
            If a file shows no coverage at all, check the following:
        </p>
        <list>
            <li>Your CI uploaded a coverage report to Codecov for the default branch, and the report includes the file.</li>
            <li>The file paths in the report match the paths in the Git repository.</li>
            <li>Coverage is not hidden: right-click in the editor and look for <control>Show Codecov Coverage</control>.</li>
            <li>The project is connected and the repository is detected in <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov</ui-path>.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            To see the coverage effect of your current branch, use the <a href="Codecov-Metrics.topic">Codecov Metrics dashboard</a> or <a href="Codecov-Folder-Coverage.topic">folder coverage</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Why is no repository detected?" id="no-repository-detected">
        <p>
            The settings page shows "No repository detected. Please verify your project settings.", or <control>Test Connection</control> reports that it could not detect the repository.
        </p>
        <list>
            <li>Make sure the project is a Git repository with a remote that points to GitHub, GitLab or Bitbucket.</li>
            <li>Make sure <control>Service Provider</control> matches the host of that remote.</li>
            <li>Make sure the repository is activated on Codecov and your token's account can access it.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="How do I fix a failed connection test?" id="auth-errors">
        <p>
            <control>Connection Test Failed</control> with "Connection failed. Please check your token." usually means the API token is wrong, revoked or expired, or <control>Server URL</control> is wrong.
        </p>
        <procedure title="Replace the API token" id="refresh-token">
            <step>Create a new API token in Codecov.</step>
            <step>Go to <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov</ui-path>.</step>
            <step>Paste the token into <control>API Token</control> and click <control>Test Connection</control>.</step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            For a self-hosted Codecov server, check that <control>Server URL</control> is the base URL of that server.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Does the plugin support private repositories?" id="private-repos">
        <p>
            Yes.
            The plugin shows coverage for any repository that the account of your API token can access on Codecov.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Why is the Codecov Metrics button disabled?" id="metrics-disabled">
        <p>
            The <control>Codecov Metrics</control> button is enabled after the plugin detects the project's Codecov repository.
            Connect the project as described in <a href="Codecov-Installation.topic"/>, then reopen the project if needed.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Why does the dashboard show no pull request impact?" id="no-pr-impact">
        <p>
            The dashboard shows "No Codecov compare report available for the current branch." in these cases:
        </p>
        <list>
            <li>You are on the default branch, which has nothing to compare.</li>
            <li>Codecov has no processed commit of the current branch yet.
                Push the branch and wait for CI to upload coverage, then click <control>Refresh</control>.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Why are there no coverage dots on folders?" id="folder-dots-missing">
        <list>
            <li>Folder coverage is off by default.
                Turn on <control>Show Coverage on Folders</control> on the Codecov Metrics toolbar.</li>
            <li>Codecov has no report for the current branch.
                The warning "Codecov: no coverage data for this branch" appears when you turn the feature on.</li>
            <li>The folder has no files in the Codecov report.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Why can't I validate codecov.yml?" id="validation-problems">
        <list>
            <li>
                "Codecov API token is missing. Please configure it in Settings." means that validation needs the API token.
                Set it as described in <a href="Codecov-Installation.topic"/>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <control>Validate Codecov YAML</control> is available only for files named exactly <path>codecov.yml</path> or <path>codecov.yaml</path>.
                Completion also works in files such as <path>.codecov.yml</path>, but validation does not.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="How do I report a bug?" id="codecov_report_bug">
        <p>
            When the IDE shows an error from the plugin, open the error details and click <control>Report Exception</control>.
            A prefilled issue opens in the <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/dorkag/issues">edgafner/dorkag repository on GitHub</a>, with the plugin, IDE and operating system versions.
            Add the steps that lead to the error and submit the issue.
        </p>
        <p>
            You can also open an issue directly in that repository.
            For other ways to get help, see <a href="Codecov-Reference-and-Support.topic"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

